    "both section readers match the heading line-anchored",
    _ckr.count('re.escape(heading)') >= 1 and _cfm.count('re.escape(heading)') == 1
    and 'body.split("## Verification", 1)' not in _cfm.split("Fixed as a class")[-1],
    "a bare substring split matches a PROSE MENTION of the heading — measured on a "
    "real handbook, where every reader was handed the tail of `## Procedure` and the "
    "old not-empty assertion passed on the wrong segment",
)
check(
    "wf-conform reports a missing negative case without failing the file",
    'not r.get("advisory")' in _cfm,
    "the negative-test record post-dates every handbook under it; it is reported "
    "on its own channel and must not borrow the `adopted` key, which main() uses "
